{"name":"Natural Bridge","hex":"#a29171","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"natural","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Existing in nature.","Normally associated with a particular person or thing; inherently related to the nature of a thing or creature."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A native inhabitant of a place, country, etc.","A note that is not or is no longer to be modified by an accidental."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/natural"},{"term":"bridge","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A construction or natural feature that spans a divide.","The upper bony ridge of the human nose."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be or make a bridge over something.","To span as if with a bridge."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bridge"}],"entries":[{"title":"Natural arch","blocks":[{"text":"A natural arch, natural bridge, or rock arch is a natural landform where an arch has formed with an opening underneath. Natural arches commonly form where inland cliffs, coastal cliffs, fins or stacks are subject to erosion from the sea, rivers or weathering."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Delicate_Arch_LaSalle.jpg/330px-Delicate_Arch_LaSalle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_arch","wikidata":"Q954501"},{"title":"Natural Bridge, Queensland","blocks":[{"text":"Natural Bridge is a rural locality in the City of Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia. It borders New South Wales. In the 2021 census, Natural Bridge had a population of 90 people."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Springbrook_Cave.jpg/330px-Springbrook_Cave.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_Bridge%2C_Queensland","wikidata":"Q23073758"},{"title":"Natural Bridge (Virginia)","blocks":[{"text":"Natural Bridge is a 